WEBVTT

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:31.720
<i>The seeds of worries that I thought I got 
rid of burst out my mind and sprouted</i>

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:47.950
<i>Today again, countless brambles 
spread out underfoot, awaiting me</i>

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Where do I go in order to meet you?</i>

00:00:56.410 --> 00:01:11.300
<i>Don't hold me, the thorns 
on my back will hurt you</i>

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:26.530
<i>But still, my overflowing 
emotions are searching for you</i>

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.990
"Journey"

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.470
We are entering a large dead 
spot in the system's coverage.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.290
So we somehow made our escape, huh?

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.170
Don't breathe a sigh of relief just yet.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.750
No matter what escape route we choose,

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.290
we'll certainly enter the system's 
active zone at some point.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.710
We'll worry about that when it happens.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.460
I'll leave it to you.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.180
We're now back to square one.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.950
You're not gonna struggle now, are you?

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.390
We have the same goal anyway.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.320
Where is this ship headed?

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.270
Do you have any place to go?

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.190
There's no reason for me to tell you that.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.660
There's no reason to keep 
you on this ship, either...

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.200
but, well, you're like an appendix.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.160
Appendix?

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.940
Where's that doppel?

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.960
I can't see her without a visor.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.330
Are you talking about Nessa?

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.450
I heard that she sticks to you like glue.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.130
Well, it's not like that.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:36.880
Well, doesn't matter.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.380
Hold the reins tightly so that 
she won't wander off anywhere.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.390
If you don't like me treating you as 
an appendix, you can get off any time,

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:50.850
although I haven't prepared any 
side trips for you to get off.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.440
Here.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.070
What's this?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.770
It's a parachute.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.160
It's not something you can 
experience so easily these days.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.170
Even if you land badly,

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.920
you'll just break a leg or two, that's all.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.330
Do you wanna hear how to use it?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.000
If you don't have that courage, 
then at least work, Boy.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:16.800
This can't be happening...

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.380
Cleaning is old fashioned.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.850
How should I put it... This is...

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.360
The back of the seat is still dirty.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.230
Humiliating!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.770
Geez, I said those go on 
the left shelf, didn't I?!

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.650
H-Hold on a sec. Let me rest for a moment.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.490
If you don't wanna do it, 
why don't you get off?

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.030
We don't need useless people.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:48.290
I don't remember joining 
a terrorist group, either!

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.210
Terrorists? For someone whose head is 
filled with nothing but dirty ideas,

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.670
you sure do like to assume things 
and act like you're better than us!

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.730
Righteousness is on our side.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.880
Righteousness? Are you serious...?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.630
What? If you have an objection, 
why don't you get off already?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.550
I know you don't have the courage for that.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.800
It's not because I don't have the courage.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.280
Then what? Why aren't you getting off?

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.660
"Why"?

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:11.140
How come you're suddenly quiet? Ah...!

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.190
You're thinking about something 
naughty again, aren't you?!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:22.150
<i>I was thinking... though 
nothing naughty... probably...</i>

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.820
Thanks.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.520
Is this your first time doing laundry, too?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.650
It's nice to be young, huh? 
Many first-time experiences.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.360
Doesn't it feel good?

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.610
You wash the clothes clean after you sweat,

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.830
and then you work more and sweat again.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.830
We repeat that over and over.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:14.790
Oh?

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:17.830
Your pants are dirty, too.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:18.960
What? Really?

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.440
Now, go ahead and take them off.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.130
Huh? N-Now?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.800
We've got clean pants for you, too, so...

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.560
That's not the poi...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.770
Here.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.470
You don't have to feel embarrassed.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.470
Hey, let me go.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.250
Really... Um, sorry. Hey! Wait!

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.060
Oh! Oh!

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.940
What's that?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.280
I-I imitated what I saw in an old book.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.990
I don't know what that is...

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.200
but you sure are a man.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.330
Then make that one next.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.010
I'll go bring more.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:13.260
Who are you playing with?

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.120
Nessa.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.640
Hm? She went somewhere.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.090
Nessa! You're here, right, Nessa?!

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.520
Just how long do you have to keep sulking?

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.490
<i>She could see her, but I couldn't.</i>

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.990
<i>Is it because she hates me now?</i>

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.450
Nessa! Come out!

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:37.370
Obsidian in the south agreed to accept us.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.080
We're gonna head there now.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.330
Do you always eat together?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.920
Yeah, unless something is going on.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.630
The food tastes better 
when you talk over dinner.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.010
Is that right?

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.140
Are you working, Boy?

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.580
How do you feel? Don't you get 
a real sense of being alive?

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.310
Along with the hardship of living.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.730
Even if we half-heartedly try 
to teach him physical labor,

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:06.070
it's virtually impossible to rehabilitate 
someone once they've learned bad customs.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.400
I'm just making him earn his 
keep while he's on this ship.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:12.030
I'm not thinking of rehabilitating 
him or anything.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.910
That's fine then.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:14.990
Not yet.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.320
Say a prayer.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.240
Prayer? To the temple?

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.210
Some things aren't funny even as a joke.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.520
She means to something more noble...

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:29.370
though I don't like that 
kind of stuff, either.

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:30.630
But...

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.660
Well, if humans need someone 
to pray to no matter what,

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:35.720
that's fine.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.870
The temple is just taking advantage of it.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:42.770
Where's Phryne?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.270
I told her to join us, but...

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.110
It's only natural that she'd have 
a hard time getting used to this...

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.890
unlike a certain someone 
who has no principals.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.620
<i>If you're around, come out, Nessa!</i>

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.310
<i>Think only about Nessa!</i>

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.170
<i>I tried what she said.</i>

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.170
<i>I'm getting upset for some reason.</i>

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.060
Phryne...

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.860
I-I'm sorry! I didn't mean to peek on you.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.370
I was told that I could pick and wear any 
clothes that are hung around here, so...

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.320
B-By those women?

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.680
The busybodies?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.160
Do I look weird?

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.450
Ah, no...

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:53.010
You look very good in them.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.620
Nessa doesn't?

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.000
She's around, but doesn't come out.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:28.920
I thought as much.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.210
What do you mean by that?

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:34.460
Nessa may be jealous.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.130
Jealous?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.010
She's attached to you.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.940
Well, I don't know if 
attached is the right word,

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.810
more like she's toying with me.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:44.560
But jealous...?

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.310
I wonder if she is.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.420
You like those, don't you?

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:07.830
I first thought Nessa was 
your doppel... but...

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:17.970
Did you... Did you take the brooch 
Nessa was in without permission?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.840
Is that why they're after you?

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:25.330
That weird guy said "the 
world's beloved maidens."

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.140
What does that mean?

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.900
I'm sorry to ask you so many questions,

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:33.360
but I just can't stop 
thinking about those things.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.860
Please answer just one question.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.800
Do you... hate Nessa?

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:46.120
I'm not supposed to like her.

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:48.260
What do you mean?!

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.890
I don't get it.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:59.490
Don't you think it's kind of hot?

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.480
Well, it's been hot for a while now.

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:07.540
What's the matter?

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.480
The temperature in the ship is going up.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.190
There's a problem somewhere in our system.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:13.180
What do you mean "somewhere"?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.440
Can you fix it quickly, Gramps?

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.230
Don't be so rattled.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:20.610
Something like this cures my boredom.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:25.040
What's up with this heat? 
Did something happen?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.990
As I thought, this is the coolest place.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:31.900
Hey! What are you two doing, 
hanging around together?

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:34.040
Not again!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.460
Whoa! Naughty stuff again?!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:39.700
No wonder it's so hot.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.760
This is no time for such a 
friendly atmosphere, is it?!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.820
At any rate, it's hot.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:46.300
I think I'll take off my clothes!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.230
Don't show me your ugly body.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.810
H... Hey!

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.020
Something wrong?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.570
Did something happen?!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.290
It's none of your business.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.770
Trouble? If there's something 
I can do to help...

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.830
Kick him out, Daidara. 
He'll infect the system.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.640
I will start the check up.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:17.710
Expose your genital area and 
sit down in the correct angle.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:19.940
That's none of your business.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.910
What an amazing patchwork!

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:30.900
So they took apart several broken 
balloons and rebuilt them...

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.560
On top of that, they did it by 
using old technologies on purpose.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.940
This is getting more complicated.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:42.400
Do you think it's an error occurring 
on the pre-Fractale system?

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:43.950
Hmm...

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.440
This is amazing!

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.680
There're many layers of 
systems that were added

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.910
one improvement after another.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.930
This goes all the way back to pre-Fractale.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:56.080
Even if I find the problem, 
it'll be very hard to hack in.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.630
Use as many methods as you can look up.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.670
If we keep tracing using old algorithms,

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.130
we'll find out where the 
error is occurring for sure.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:04.550
Yes.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.970
Even a 26th century patch doesn't work.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.750
Then...

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:11.350
What's this?!

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.230
What's this noise?

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:15.990
It's moving.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:17.730
Please hear me out!

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.660
You again? Don't bother us.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.160
What is it? Tell us.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.040
You've noticed the noise, right?

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.710
It might be Nessa.

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:25.450
Nessa?

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:29.840
I saw a similar noise pattern 
when I took out Nessa.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.060
Don't be ridiculous.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:34.660
This noise showed up when 
we traced an old program.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.330
Are you saying that that doppel 
is data with old components?

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.540
That I don't know, but...

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:44.770
So you think Nessa is causing this trouble?

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:45.810
Probably.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:46.760
Seriously?

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.980
What a troublemaker she is.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:51.430
What's the matter?!

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.430
The auto pilot isn't functioning properly.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.310
We're going into thunderclouds.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.730
Start evasive maneuvers now!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.440
I am... but most of the 
controls aren't functioning.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.780
Can't you call out Nessa?

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.490
I can't. Nessa is sulking and hiding.

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.780
Sulking? What'd you do?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.120
Nothing.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.340
Dated two girls and made a blunder?

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:14.540
Wha...

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.040
Anyway, it seems that restoring 
that mademoiselle's good spirits

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.250
is the only way to fix this situation.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.590
I'm practically being roasted in this heat.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.760
Please open the windows.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.180
Can't you see? It's storming outside.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.750
This is like being in a sauna.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:33.280
You'll lose weight.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.390
This is the world's worst heat endurance 
contest, and we can't get out of it

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.600
even if we throw in the towel...

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.940
There's something we have to do 
before throwing in the towel.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:42.690
Find Nessa.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.320
In order to resolve this situation now,

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.530
we need to find Nessa, 
who's hiding somewhere.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.570
Nessa? What is she?

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.440
She's quite a troublemaker,

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:54.990
but she's an important doppel.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:58.540
Doesn't matter. If it'll cool 
down the ship, let's find her.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:01.080
But how do we find her?

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.430
I'll chase Nessa's data 
and give you instructions.

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:06.450
Also, if we do something she likes...

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.300
something that interests her

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.470
I'm sure she'll come out.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:13.550
Then, I'll use all my skills to 
make delicious food or something.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.310
Well, she's a doppel, so...

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:20.560
Ah... She, one time, asked me 
to explain "tasty" by dancing.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.810
Dancing, he said. Dancing.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.570
Ah, let's see... There, there.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:28.480
That's not good. Do it more cheerfully.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:33.740
There, there, there, there...!

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:36.080
Like this? How about like this?!

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:42.080
I don't think that's quite 
what I was talking about...

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.010
I'm being crushed...

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:05.150
What're you guys doing in the 
confusion of the moment?!

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.190
Wonderful! Wonderful!

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.820
Nessa likes the shove and 
push game. It seems warm.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.790
Well, it's already hot without playing it.

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:18.080
Ah! There she is! Nessa!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.580
Nessa?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.060
Nessa?

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.080
Sorry!

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.630
She's in the storage right 
now... Ah! She disappeared!

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:32.340
This time, she's in the kitchen.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.310
This time, the C-3 pathway.

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:44.480
Nessa! Come out, Nessa!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.500
Nessa!

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:55.450
There you are, beloved maidens.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.790
That girl...!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.200
As I thought, they are together.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:08.380
Let's get her back first.

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:13.130
She disappeared again.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:16.990
Is she really still sulking? Or...

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:18.440
What're you doing?

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:19.720
Don't do such a foolish thing.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:24.850
Hey! Don't do things without permission! 
You're still in captivity, you know!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.730
"In captivity"...? Phryne?!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.770
Open the door!

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:30.940
Come out.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.900
Hey! Are you listening?!

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:33.900
Phryne!

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.700
That's no use!

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.480
The hatch won't open due 
to the system trouble!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.620
Come back, Phryne!

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:47.580
Nessa doesn't come out 
because I'm around. So...

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:49.040
You're wrong.

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:52.460
Nessa probably has even forgotten 
that she was sulking.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:53.720
What?

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:56.450
She's forgotten why she was hiding

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:58.970
and now she's just having 
fun playing hide-and-seek.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:01.000
Nessa is carefree like that, so...

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.350
That's why I didn't want you to 
bring her out from the brooch.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.220
Why?

00:18:05.030 --> 00:18:08.520
Seeing her before my eyes is painful.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.270
What do you mean?

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:14.230
To the temple, Nessa is 
more important than me.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:18.320
So... I wanted to take her with me 
so we could end everything together.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:21.070
End? Why?

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:25.500
To us, ending this foolish 
repetition is the only way to...

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.620
No... That can't be the answer!

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.560
If you end it, nothing will start.

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:32.710
You can't find anything new!

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:37.660
I think, to Nessa, every moment is new...

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.510
just like a newborn baby.

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.260
So everything is fun for her.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.310
Me, too... After getting onboard this ship,

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.930
sometimes I feel like it's kinda fun.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.830
This was unexpected,

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:54.570
but it's fun to be able to see 
what I couldn't see before.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:59.120
I felt kinda free. So Nessa is free.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.740
With the right frame of mind, 
Phryne, you too, will...

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:01.730
Don't say...

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:02.200
What?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.380
Don't say irresponsible things.

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:08.910
You don't understand anything at all.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.210
Then explain it to me!

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.250
How am I supposed to understand 
it when you don't tell me?!

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.710
Just... leave me alone!

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.800
Ah... Phryne! Phryne! Phryne!

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:23.550
Phryne! Phryne!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.690
Phryne?

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.580
Are you hiding, too?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:49.900
Nessa...

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:55.130
No? Are you sad?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.470
Nessa dislikes "being sad," too.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.430
That's not it. I'm just hiding.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:05.720
Hide-and-seek?!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:08.390
But I've been found.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:11.140
You've been found? By who?

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.610
By you, Nessa.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:14.850
You're it, Nessa.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.470
It? Was Nessa it?

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:21.240
Then it's okay for Nessa to find Phryne?

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.700
If you're okay with it...

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:29.080
Nessa found Phryne!

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.250
Just finding me wouldn't do.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:35.130
You grab my hand and take me to everyone.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.080
Okay!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.220
Nessa caught Phryne!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.200
<i>When Phryne brought Nessa...</i>

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.470
<i>No, I mean, when Nessa brought Phryne,</i>

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:50.660
<i>the alarmist hide-and-seek ended</i>

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.480
<i>and the system recovered without incident.</i>

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:57.730
<i>Since then, Nessa settled down on 
the ship as if it was just natural.</i>

00:20:57.730 --> 00:20:59.900
<i>As for what else has changed, 
well, that would be...</i>

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:03.740
<i>that Phryne started eating 
with everyone else,</i>

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:06.950
<i>that she smiles a little 
more often than before,</i>

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:12.160
<i>that they no longer tell me to leave 
when I watch gauges at the cockpit,</i>

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:13.870
<i>and...</i>

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.150
<i>that cloth for my crotch...</i>

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.380
Hey, hey... Wait! Hey!

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:22.060
<i>Is now red.</i>

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:37.480
<i>The same sleepy winter afternoon 
is repeated every day</i>

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:51.930
<i>Just once, I had a dream that 
I slipped off of a salley tree</i>

00:21:52.660 --> 00:22:06.210
<i>Until the warmth you left 
behind becomes light</i>

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:20.200
<i>I will picture you in the sunny spot 
that I've grown accustomed to going to</i>

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:48.510
<i>The sunny spot that strokes 
my cheek reminds me of you</i>
